    "answer": "California's utility-scale energy market runs through Pacific Gas & Electric (PG&E), Southern California Edison (SCE), San Diego Gas & Electric (SDG&E), Los Angeles Dept. of Water & Power (LADWP). California remains the largest solar state by installed capacity — massive utility-scale plants in the Mojave and Central Valley, plus the country's deepest battery storage fleet addressing the duck curve's evening ramp. CAISO operates the wholesale market and runs the generator interconnection cluster study process. Distribution-level interconnection follows CPUC Rule 21. California's duck curve — midday solar oversupply, steep evening ramp — defines grid planning.",
